            <ArticleTitle>[Experience in perfection of outpatient pulmonological service].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>44-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="AIM" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To obtain objective information on the quality of pulmonological outpatient care for patients living in the North Administrative District (NAD) of Moscow; to propose methods of this care improvement.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="MATERIAL AND METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">An epidemiological study of Moscow NAD population was made to detect respiratory diseases, to assess qualification of district physicians in management of most prevalent chronic diseases of the respiratory system: bronchial asthma (BA) and chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD).</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">The epidemiological study has revealed standard errors of district physicians in management of BA and COPD patients. Effective measures on reduction of the typical mistakes are proposed.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">More active detection of respiratory diseases in Moscow population is recommended.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
